{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02050",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.91,
      "end_seconds": 11.61,
      "duration_seconds": 10.7,
      "text": "Sorry, you know, what was I saying, hi, doctor, I came as soon as they called me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 12.32,
      "end_seconds": 16.43,
      "duration_seconds": 4.11,
      "text": "That's fine, sit down. Tell me why you came."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 17.46,
      "end_seconds": 31.21,
      "duration_seconds": 13.75,
      "text": "Right, you know, doctor, I'll sit in if that's okay, I know what's been happening. Um, she's been having a nosebleed that won't stop, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 32.83,
      "end_seconds": 34.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.14,
      "text": "Did it come on recently?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.26,
      "end_seconds": 40.47,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "I mean, around three weeks, I think."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 41.15,
      "end_seconds": 45.57,
      "duration_seconds": 4.42,
      "text": "Actually, it was closer to a month, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 46.29,
      "end_seconds": 51.03,
      "duration_seconds": 4.74,
      "text": "Okay, so roughly three to four weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 53.04,
      "end_seconds": 55.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "That sounds about right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 56.5,
      "end_seconds": 58.11,
      "duration_seconds": 1.61,
      "text": "What brings it on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 62.78,
      "end_seconds": 67.21,
      "duration_seconds": 4.43,
      "text": "It's, It's worse with blowing the nose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 69.12,
      "end_seconds": 72.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "Have you noticed anything else alongside it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 74.21,
      "end_seconds": 96.81,
      "duration_seconds": 22.6,
      "text": "Hmm, when it starts I tend to get blood down the back of my throat as well. The blood down the back of my throat? That's been for three days. Well, um, I've also been feeling lightheaded, for two months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 97.86,
      "end_seconds": 102.34,
      "duration_seconds": 4.48,
      "text": "Do you react to any medicines or foods? Any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 104.4,
      "end_seconds": 112.55,
      "duration_seconds": 8.15,
      "text": "Years back I got feeling very drowsy from tramadol, so I stay away from it now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.36,
      "end_seconds": 115.11,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "So, do you smoke?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 115.8,
      "end_seconds": 119.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "No, I've never smoked in my life."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.6,
      "end_seconds": 123.25,
      "duration_seconds": 1.65,
      "text": "Do you drink alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 124.65,
      "end_seconds": 128.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "I only drink at family occasions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 129.79,
      "end_seconds": 131.01,
      "duration_seconds": 1.22,
      "text": "What's your work?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 133.04,
      "end_seconds": 137.39,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "I'm a plumber, lots of bending and kneeling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 138.02,
      "end_seconds": 140.01,
      "duration_seconds": 1.99,
      "text": "Do you live by yourself?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 141.13,
      "end_seconds": 145.17,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "No, I share a house with my brother."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 151.22,
      "end_seconds": 154.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "Have you been to theatre before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 154.87,
      "end_seconds": 161.78,
      "duration_seconds": 6.91,
      "text": "Just a mole taken off my arm, a few years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 163.33,
      "end_seconds": 166.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "Has anyone ever diagnosed you with something?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 169.43,
      "end_seconds": 186.35,
      "duration_seconds": 16.92,
      "text": "I mean, I've had an irregular heartbeat, yes. Uh, you know, I have an underactive thyroid, for about a year. High cholesterol, for about a year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 187.63,
      "end_seconds": 194.11,
      "duration_seconds": 6.48,
      "text": "Okay, I can see an irregular heartbeat and an underactive thyroid in your file as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 205.2,
      "end_seconds": 208.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "Which medicines do you take at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 210.56,
      "end_seconds": 225.72,
      "duration_seconds": 15.16,
      "text": "I'm on apixaban, 5 milligrams, twice a day. Thyronorm. I take it 50 micrograms, every morning. I'm on simvastatin, 20 milligrams, at night for my cholesterol."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.44,
      "end_seconds": 241.28,
      "duration_seconds": 1.84,
      "text": "How about easy bruising?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 241.92,
      "end_seconds": 244.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "No, no easy bruising."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 248.19,
      "end_seconds": 253.57,
      "duration_seconds": 5.38,
      "text": "A few quick ones: chest pain, black stools or head injury?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 254.66,
      "end_seconds": 258.82,
      "duration_seconds": 4.16,
      "text": "Erm, no, none of those at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 263.54,
      "end_seconds": 265.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "Is your digestion otherwise okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 267.9,
      "end_seconds": 270.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.14,
      "text": "No, all normal there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 271.22,
      "end_seconds": 273.19,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "Anything unusual with passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 274.33,
      "end_seconds": 278.87,
      "duration_seconds": 4.54,
      "text": "Hmm, um, no, that's all fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 293.27,
      "end_seconds": 296.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "I'll just record a few vital signs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 304.99,
      "end_seconds": 307.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "So, sit still for a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 323.95,
      "end_seconds": 332.45,
      "duration_seconds": 8.5,
      "text": "Okay: temperature 36.8, pulse is 75 beats a minute, oxygen saturation is 97 percent, pressure 114 over 82."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 334.97,
      "end_seconds": 339.03,
      "duration_seconds": 4.06,
      "text": "I'd like to check you over now, if that's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 340.76,
      "end_seconds": 343.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "Okay, tell me if that's sore."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 360.01,
      "end_seconds": 366.7,
      "duration_seconds": 6.69,
      "text": "There is a bleeding point on the front of the septum and the nose has been dry."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 370.83,
      "end_seconds": 398.42,
      "duration_seconds": 27.59,
      "text": "Okay, that's enough for me. Having listened and examined, this looks most like an anterior nosebleed on a blood thinner. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer. I'd also keep a clotting problem in mind. Stop me if I've got anything wrong. You've had a nosebleed that won't stop, and no head injury or chest pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 399.41,
      "end_seconds": 401.13,
      "duration_seconds": 1.72,
      "text": "That's it, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 406.39,
      "end_seconds": 415.85,
      "duration_seconds": 9.46,
      "text": "A blood count is what I'd like next, for epistaxis. I'm going to order a clotting test, for epistaxis on anticoagulant."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 417.34,
      "end_seconds": 418.58,
      "duration_seconds": 1.24,
      "text": "Right, understood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 421.86,
      "end_seconds": 443.18,
      "duration_seconds": 21.32,
      "text": "Lean forward and pinch the soft part of the nose for fifteen minutes; I will cauterise the point. Come back or go to emergency straight away if the bleeding does not stop after twenty minutes. We'll catch up in one week. Is there anything you'd like me to go over again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 443.78,
      "end_seconds": 449.02,
      "duration_seconds": 5.24,
      "text": "Um, you know, I think I understand everything. Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 450.89,
      "end_seconds": 452.28,
      "duration_seconds": 1.39,
      "text": "See you soon."
    }
  ]
}